    "q-99414": {
      "dom_id": "step-q99414",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=0,$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1,1,1⟩, \\\\ N(0) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively.",
      "worked_solution": "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(0) & =T(0)\\times N(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1,1,1⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨(0-1),-(0-(-1)),(1-(-1))⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨-1,-1,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-99414-a",
