    "q-99421": {
      "dom_id": "step-q99421",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=3,$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,3,4⟩, \\\\ N(3) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,4,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively.",
      "worked_solution": "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(3) & =T(3)\\times N(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,3,4⟩\\times \\frac{1}{5}⟨0,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}⟨(-9-16),-(0-0),(0-0)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}⟨-25,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
