    "q-99415": {
      "dom_id": "step-q99415",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}⟨3,5,4⟩, \\\\ N(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨4,0,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively.",
      "worked_solution": "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =T(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)\\times N(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}⟨3,5,4⟩\\times \\frac{1}{5}⟨4,0,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25\\sqrt{2}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25\\sqrt{2}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25\\sqrt{2}}⟨(-15-0),-(-9-16),(0-20)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25\\sqrt{2}}⟨-15,25,-20⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}⟨-3,5,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-99415-a",
