    "q-127694": {
      "dom_id": "step-q127694",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t,\\,-1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector.",
      "worked_solution": "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nN(t)=\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t,\\,0,\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{(-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t)^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{25{sin}^{2}⁡5t+25{cos}^{2}⁡5t} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t,\\,0,\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t⟩}{(\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}})}=⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t,\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t,\\,-1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t⟩\\times ⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t,\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡5t & -1 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t & 0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡5t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡5t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡5t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t & -1 \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t-0,-({cos}^{2}⁡5t+{sin}^{2}⁡5t),0-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t,\\,-1,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
