    "q-99651": {
      "dom_id": "step-q99651",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5}}⟨2t,\\,2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector.",
      "worked_solution": "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nN(t)=\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{10}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}},\\,-\\frac{8t}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}},\\,\\frac{4t}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}}⟨5,\\,-4t,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{2}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{(5)^{2}+(-4t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{25+16{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{20{t}^{2}+25} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{4{t}^{2}+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{2}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}}⟨5,\\,-4t,\\,2t⟩}{(\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{4{t}^{2}+5})}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5}}⟨5,\\,-4t,\\,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5}}⟨2t,2,-1⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5}}⟨5,\\,-4t,\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}(4{t}^{2}+5)}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2t & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -4t & 2t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}(4{t}^{2}+5)}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4t & 2t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}2t & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}2t & 2 \\\\ 5 & -4t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}(4{t}^{2}+5)}⟨4t-4t,-(4{t}^{2}+5),-8{t}^{2}-10⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}(4{t}^{2}+5)}⟨0,\\,-(4{t}^{2}+5),\\,-2(4{t}^{2}+5)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨0,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
